{"name":"Industrial Revolution","hex":"#737373","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Industrial Revolution","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The major technological, socioeconomic and cultural change in the late 18th and early 19th century resulting from the replacement of an economy based on manual labour to one dominated by industry and machine manufacture."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Industrial_Revolution"}],"entries":[{"title":"Industrial Revolution","blocks":[{"text":"The Industrial Revolution, sometimes called the First Industrial Revolution in contrast to the subsequent Second Industrial Revolution, was a transitional period of the global economy toward more widespread, efficient and stable manufacturing processes, succeeding the Second Agricultural Revolution. Beginning in Great Britain around 1760, the Industrial Revolution had spread to continental Europe and the United States by about 1840. Economic historians agree that the onset of the Industrial Revolution is the most important event in human history, comparable only to the adoption of agriculture for material advancement."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Powerloom_weaving_in_1835.jpg/330px-Powerloom_weaving_in_1835.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Industrial_Revolution","wikidata":"Q2269"},{"title":"Revolution","blocks":[{"text":"In political science, a revolution is a rapid, fundamental transformation of a society's class, state, ethnic, or religious structures. According to the sociologist Jack Goldstone, all revolutions contain \"a common set of elements at their core: (a) efforts to change the political regime that draw on a competing vision of a just order, (b) a notable degree of informal or formal mass mobilization, and (c) efforts to force change through noninstitutionalized actions such as mass demonstrations, protests, strikes, or violence.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/La_Libert%C3%A9_guidant_le_peuple_-_Eug%C3%A8ne_Delacroix_-_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_Peintures_RF_129_-_apr%C3%A8s_restauration_2024.jpg/330px-La_Libert%C3%A9_guidant_le_peuple_-_Eug%C3%A8ne_Delacroix_-_Mus%C3%A9e_du_Louvre_Peintures_RF_129_-_apr%C3%A8s_restauration_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revolution","wikidata":"Q10931"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Hand-loom_weaving_%28Bonhams%29.jpg/500px-Hand-loom_weaving_%28Bonhams%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Hand-loom_weaving_%28Bonhams%29.jpg/1280px-Hand-loom_weaving_%28Bonhams%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Hand-loom_weaving_%28Bonhams%29.jpg/500px-Hand-loom_weaving_%28Bonhams%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Weaving with handlooms from William Hogarth's Industry and Idleness in 1747","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHand-loom_weaving_(Bonhams).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Silkmill1.jpg/500px-Silkmill1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Silkmill1.jpg/500px-Silkmill1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"John Lombe's silk mill site today in Derby, rebuilt as Derby Silk Mill","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilkmill1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Colonisation_1754.png/500px-Colonisation_1754.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, ht